      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white border-b border-slate-800 pb-2">
        Contractual Traps: The One-Way Ratchet Policy &amp; Annual Lock-In Penalties
      </h2>
      <p>
        The most punishing legal condition governing HubSpot Marketing Hub contracts is what industry insiders call the <strong>One-Way Ratchet</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        If your marketing contact tier threshold is 25,000 and an uncurated CSV import or viral marketing surge brings your count to 25,001 on the 14th of the month, HubSpot automatically bills your credit card for the next 5,000-contact pack. However, even if your marketing operations lead immediately identifies the duplicate contacts and deletes 10,000 inactive leads the very next morning:
      </p>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-slate-300 list-disc pl-5">
        <li><strong>No Mid-Term Downgrades</strong>: HubSpot policy strictly forbids lowering your billed marketing contact tier during your active 12-month agreement.</li>
        <li><strong>Mandatory Prepayment Obligation</strong>: You are legally bound to pay for that expanded tier for every remaining month of your annual contract.</li>
        <li><strong>Automatic Renewal Defaults</strong>: Unless formal written notice of downgrade or cancellation is submitted exactly 30 to 60 days prior to contract expiration, the account automatically auto-renews at the highest peak contact rate achieved during the prior year.</li>
      </ul>

