        Decoupled Open-Source Architecture: Twenty CRM, Mautic, and Amazon SES
      </h2>
      <p>
        The modern architectural solution to avoiding SaaS contact taxation is <strong>decoupling relational CRM records from message delivery pipelines</strong>. Instead of storing all contacts inside an all-in-one commercial platform that charges you rent for every row in their database, deploy a modular three-tier open-source infrastructure:
      </p>
      <ol class="space-y-3 text-slate-300 list-decimal pl-5">
        <li><strong>Twenty CRM (Relational Pipeline Tier)</strong>: An open-source, modern TypeScript/NestJS CRM backed by PostgreSQL. Manages lead stages, company associations, deals, and notes with zero contact tier limits.</li>
        <li><strong>Mautic (Marketing Automation Tier)</strong>: An enterprise-grade, self-hosted open-source marketing automation platform. Handles landing page forms, behavioral lead scoring, dynamic segments, and multi-step drip email workflows.</li>
        <li><strong>Amazon Simple Email Service (SES) (Delivery Engine)</strong>: Cloud infrastructure sending bulk transactional and marketing emails at <strong>$0.10 per 1,000 emails</strong> ($100 per 1,000,000 emails sent), featuring dedicated IP routing and automated DKIM/DMARC signing.</li>
      </ol>

